Task 4: Control Flow Practice

Suppose we want to characterize the post-treatment (or placebo) blood pressure measurement as optimal (≤ 120), borderline (120 &lt; bp ≤ 130), and high (&gt; 130). First, create a new column in each data frame from above called status. You can do this via

your_df$status &lt;- character(20) #or 10 depending on number of observations



bp_list$treatment$status &lt;- character(20)
bp_list$placebo$status &lt;- character(10)


For the non-placebo data frame (within the list), create a for loop and use if/then/else logic to create the status column’s values.


for (i in 1:nrow(bp_list$treatment)) {
  if (bp_list$treatment$bp_post[i] &lt;= 120) {
    bp_list$treatment$status[i] &lt;- "Optimal"
  } else if (bp_list$treatment$bp_post[i] &lt;= 130) {
    bp_list$treatment$status[i] &lt;- "Borderline"
  } else {
    bp_list$treatment$status[i] &lt;- "High"
  }
}


Repeat for the placebo data frame (within the list).


for (i in 1:nrow(bp_list$placebo)) {
  if (bp_list$placebo$bp_post[i] &lt;=  120) {
    bp_list$placebo$status[i] &lt;- "Optimal"
  } else if (bp_list$placebo$bp_post[i] &lt;= 130) {
    bp_list$placebo$status[i] &lt;- "Borderline"
  } else {
    bp_list$placebo$status[i] &lt;- "High"
  }
}

## Task 4: Control Flow Practice
Create a new column in each data frame called status:

bpList$treatment$status &lt;- character(20)
bpList$placebo$status &lt;- character(10)

Use a for loop and if/else logic to fill the status column of the treatment data frame with “optimal”, “borderline”, or “high” based on the post-treatment blood pressure measurement:

for (patient in 1:dim(bpList$treatment)[1]) {
  if (bpList$treatment$postBP[patient] &lt;= 120) {
    bpList$treatment$status[patient] &lt;- 'optimal'
    }
  else if (bpList$treatment$postBP[patient] &gt; 130) {
    bpList$treatment$status[patient] &lt;- 'high'
    }
  else {
    bpList$treatment$status[patient] &lt;- 'borderline'
    }
}

Use a for loop and if/else logic to fill the status column of the placebo data frame with “optimal”, “borderline”, or “high” based on the post-treatment blood pressure measurement:

for (patient in 1:dim(bpList$placebo)[1]) {
  if (bpList$placebo$postBP[patient] &lt;= 120) {
    bpList$placebo$status[patient] &lt;- 'optimal'
    }
  else if (bpList$placebo$postBP[patient] &gt; 130) {
    bpList$placebo$status[patient] &lt;- 'high'
    }
  else {
    bpList$placebo$status[patient] &lt;- 'borderline'
    }
}

